    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i checked the vents and they seem fine, they're blowing air. i was thinking maybe there's something inside the walls or in the ductwork itself causing a blockage or something? like it's just not getting the air to that one spot properly. what else could be hiding in there causing issues?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A partial blockage or leak in the ductwork leading to the master bedroom is a very plausible culprit. Leaky ducts can allow conditioned air to escape into unconditioned spaces like attics or crawlspaces, reducing airflow to the intended room. Another possibility is that the zone damper controlling that specific bedroom might be stuck or partially closed, restricting the flow of cool air. Having an HVAC professional inspect the ductwork visually is the best way to diagnose internal issues.",
      "source": "target",
