      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah that makes sense. could it be something actually stuck in the ducts like debris or maybe like a small animal? just trying to figure out if i need to call a pro or if i can just poke around and find the blockage myself.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is generally not recommended to attempt poking around in the ductwork yourself, as this can worsen any blockage or cause damage. Debris or small animal obstructions can sometimes get lodged deep inside and require professional equipment to remove safely. If you suspect a severe blockage or are unsure of the cause, calling an HVAC technician is the safest and most effective next step. They have the tools to safely inspect the entire system and pinpoint the exact issue.",
      "source": "target",
